f:Tacc,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"When did Adi Shankaracharya live?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Traditional dates place Shankaracharya between 788–820 CE, though some scholars argue for earlier dates. He lived only 32 years — an astonishing brevity given his philosophical output."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What did Shankaracharya teach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Shankaracharya systematized Advaita Vedanta — the philosophy of non-dualism. His central teaching: Brahman alone is real; the individual soul (Atman) and the universe are not separate from Brahman. Apparent multiplicity is Maya."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the four Mathas established by Shankaracharya?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The four cardinal monasteries: Sringeri (South), Puri (East), Dwaraka (West), and Jyotirmath (North). Each oversees one of the four Vedas and is headed by a Shankaracharya in the lineage — a tradition unbroken for 1,200 years."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What major texts did Shankaracharya write?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"His commentaries on the Upanishads, Bhagavad Gita, and Brahma Sutras are definitive. His independent works include Vivekachudamani (The Crest Jewel of Discrimination), Atma Bodha, and devotional hymns like Bhaja Govindam."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why is Shankaracharya called 'Adi'?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"'Adi' means 'first' or 'original.' He is Adi Shankaracharya to distinguish him from later teachers in his lineage who took the title Shankaracharya. He is the originator."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Digvijaya — Shankaracharya's journey?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Digvijaya (conquest of directions) was Shankaracharya's journey across India on foot, debating scholars of every school — Mimamsakas, Buddhists, Jains, Shaivas — and establishing Advaita as the preeminent philosophical system."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How did Shankaracharya unify Hinduism?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"He established the Shanmata system — the worship of six deities (Shiva, Vishnu, Devi, Ganesha, Surya, Skanda) as different manifestations of the one Brahman. This gave seekers of different temperaments a unified framework."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Shankaracharya relevant today?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Completely. His commentaries are still the primary texts studied in Sanskrit philosophy courses. His analysis of consciousness, identity, and liberation reads as incisively as ever. Figures like Ramana Maharshi and Swami Vivekananda worked directly within his framework."}}]}7:["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"min-h-screen bg-background text-foreground selection:bg-orange-500/30 selection:text-orange-100 flex flex-col","children":[["$","$Le",null,{"slug":"adi-shankaracharya-life-teachings","pillar":"ancient-wisdom"}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"$f"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"Who is Adi Shankaracharya? His Life, Philosophy & Legacy\",\"description\":\"Adi Shankaracharya (788–820 CE) was the philosopher who unified Sanatan Dharma, defeated every school of thought in debate, and wrote commentaries that remain definitive after 1,200 years.\",\"url\":\"https://opensadhaka.com/adi-shankaracharya-life-teachings\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://opensadhaka.com/adi-shankaracharya-life-teachings\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-03-04\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-03-04\",\"articleSection\":\"Ancient Wisdom\",\"keywords\":[\"adi shankaracharya biography\"],\"about\":[{\"@type\":\"Thing\",\"name\":\"adi shankaracharya biography\"}],\"isPartOf\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"name\":\"Ancient Wisdom\",\"url\":\"https://opensadhaka.com/ancient-wisdom-philosophies\"},\"inLanguage\":\"en\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Sadhaka\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"Sadhaka\",\"url\":\"https://opensadhaka.com\"}}"}}],"$L10","$L11","$L12"]}],["$L13","$L14"],"$L15"]}]
