19:[["$","title","0",{"children":"Who is Adi Shankaracharya? His Life, Philosophy & Legacy | Sadhaka | Sadhaka"}],["$","meta","1",{"name":"description","content":"Adi Shankaracharya (788–820 CE) was the philosopher who unified Sanatan Dharma, defeated every school of thought in debate, and wrote commentaries that remain definitive after 1,200 years."}],["$","link","2",{"rel":"author","href":"https://opensadhaka.com"}],["$","meta","3",{"name":"author","content":"Sadhaka"}],["$","meta","4",{"name":"keywords","content":"sanatan dharma,bhagavad gita,vedas,upanishads,yoga philosophy,sanskrit,spiritual guidance,vedanta,sadhana,meditation,spiritual practices"}],["$","meta","5",{"name":"creator","content":"Sadhaka"}],["$","meta","6",{"name":"publisher","content":"Sadhaka"}],["$","meta","7",{"name":"robots","content":"index, follow"}],["$","meta","8",{"name":"googlebot","content":"index, follow, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1"}],["$","link","9",{"rel":"canonical","href":"https://opensadhaka.com/adi-shankaracharya-life-teachings"}],["$","meta","10",{"name":"format-detection","content":"telephone=no, address=no, email=no"}],["$","meta","11",{"property":"og:title","content":"Who is Adi Shankaracharya? His Life, Philosophy & Legacy"}],["$","meta","12",{"property":"og:description","content":"Adi Shankaracharya (788–820 CE) was the philosopher who unified Sanatan Dharma, defeated every school of thought in debate, and wrote commentaries that remain definitive after 1,200 years."}],["$","meta","13",{"property":"og:url","content":"https://opensadhaka.com/adi-shankaracharya-life-teachings"}],["$","meta","14",{"property":"og:site_name","content":"Sadhaka"}],["$","meta","15",{"property":"og:locale","content":"en_US"}],["$","meta","16",{"property":"og:type","content":"article"}],["$","meta","17",{"property":"article:published_time","content":"2026-03-04"}],["$","meta","18",{"name":"twitter:card","content":"summary_large_image"}],["$","meta","19",{"name":"t